 "transcript": {
  "answer": "The advertised standard variable rate for owner-occupiers is about **4.4 percentage points above the cash rate**.\n\n- **Standard variable home loan rate (owner-occupier):** 8.77% per year in September 2026 (RBA table F5).\n- **Cash rate target:** 4.36% (monthly average for September 2026).\n- **Gap:** 8.77 − 4.36 = **4.41 percentage points**.\n\nThe gap has barely moved over the past year and a half. It was 4.42 points in January 2025 (8.77% vs 4.35%) and 4.42 points in January 2026 (8.02% vs 3.60%). Banks have passed the cash rate changes through in full, so the spread has stayed roughly constant.",
